&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-fallback" data-lang="fallback"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;I prefer the angular armour of the Lucius pattern titans rather than the rounded armour of the official GW miniatures, so I designed this Knight-size titan to be compatible with Adeptus Titanicus scale.
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;It is slightly larger than the GW Knight miniatures, so you could scale it down a bit if you prefer to be more exact. I like the chunky look. For use in Epic you would need to scale down even further - not sure the exact proportion (see &amp;#39;Alternate Scale Prints&amp;#39; section below).
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;This is designed to be very easy to print. All parts except the legs can be printed without supports. I would be open to any ideas about how to redesign the legs to print without supports (I have considered making them multipart). I&amp;#39;ve had good success printing at both 0.06 and 0.1 resolution, with 10-20% infill.
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;There are three weapon options and two leg options. The banner between the legs is optional. I hope to design some more heads and some weapons for use as Cerastus.
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
